{"beat": 5, "name": "THE MAILBOX AT THE END OF THE LANE", "text": "One piece had to come first, and the post office built it. For most of the century, a farm family collected its mail in town, when somebody had a reason to go. On October 1, 1896, the post office tried something new around Charles Town, Halltown and Uvilla, West Virginia: carriers who took the mail out to the farms themselves. Rural Free Delivery. It became permanent on July 1, 1902. The country went from under 500 rural carriers to over 32,000 in a handful of years. So by the time anyone argued about parcels, the farm had something it had never had: a mailbox at the end of the lane, and a carrier who came to it on a route. What it didn't have was a way to send anything heavy down that lane.", "provider": "placeholder", "words": [{"word": "One", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.22}, {"word": "piece", "start": 0.22, "end": 0.5}, {"word": "had", "start": 0.5, "end": 0.76}, {"word": "to", "start": 0.76, "end": 0.9}, {"word": "come", "start": 0.9, "end": 1.08}, {"word": "first,", "start": 1.08, "end": 1.44}, {"word": "and", "start": 1.44, "end": 1.64}, {"word": "the", "start": 1.64, "end": 1.78}, {"word": "post", "start": 1.78, "end": 2.0}, {"word": "office", "start": 2.0, "end": 2.32}, {"word": "built", "start": 2.32, "end": 2.68}, {"word": "it.", "start": 2.68, "end": 2.88}, {"word": "For", "start": 3.36, "end": 3.54}, {"word": "most", "start": 3.54, "end": 3.8}, {"word": "of", "start": 3.8, "end": 3.94}, {"word": "the", "start": 3.94, "end": 4.04}, {"word": "century,", "start": 4.04, "end": 4.44}, {"word": "a", "start": 4.8, "end": 4.98}, {"word": "farm", "start": 4.98, "end": 5.32}, {"word": "family", "start": 5.32, "end": 5.78}, {"word": "collected", "start": 5.78, "end": 6.24}, {"word": "its", "start": 6.24, "end": 6.46}, {"word": "mail", "start": 6.46, "end": 6.76}, {"word": "in", "start": 6.76, "end": 6.94}, {"word": "town,", "start": 6.94, "end": 7.32}, {"word": "when", "start": 7.32, "end": 7.84}, {"word